Original commit body from b0af51d815b7e0aea74fdd52ed5b66e6fd37698f:

`hypergumbo sketch` printed a concept-detected data model as
`Author (django django model)`. The concept detector composed the
framework into the label ("django model") and the formatter prefixed
DataModel.framework again. The formatter's own tests already built
DataModels with label="model", framework="Django", so the producer was
what broke the contract.

- datamodels._detect_from_concepts: the label names the construct only
  ("model" / "schema" / "entity"); framework-less labels unchanged.
- sketch._datamodel_description composes "{framework} {label}" once,
  for grouped AND fallback lines. The fallback used to print the label
  alone, which after the label change would have lost the framework.

Live, production CLI, Django + Pydantic fixture: before
`Author (django django model)`; after `Author (django model)`.

Not in this change, filed as WI-kiluh: the item's unchecked lead holds.
`BookSchema(BaseModel)` reads `(Schema)` because
_detect_from_base_classes reads meta["parent_bases"], which no analyzer
emits (they emit base_classes), so that strategy never fires. Turning
it on changes detection output, so it is measured first there.

Addresses WI-kibat.

